<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kaska</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 BCE – 1100 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Kaska, tribal peoples of the Pontic mountains who for three centuries raided the Hittite heartland and once burned Hattusa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kaska lived in the wooded mountains between the Hittite heartland and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. They appear in Hittite texts from the 15th century BCE, when they overran the holy city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nerik">Nerik</a> and pushed into central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were not a state but groups of villages under local chiefs, living from herding and farming and raiding Hittite lands. Hittite kings made short-lived treaties with individual groups. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mursili-ii">Mursili II</a> wrote that one chief, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pihhuniya">Pihhuniya</a>, ruled not in the Kaska way but like a king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kaska raiders sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> in the 14th century BCE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-iii">Hattusili III</a> only recovered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nerik">Nerik</a> in the 13th. After the Hittite collapse they moved south-east, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-i">Tiglath-Pileser I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> fought them c. 1100 BCE; then they vanish.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 1450 BCE – 1100 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:30.85%;width:6.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 BCE – 1100 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century-bce">15th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pihhuniya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kaskians, Gasga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1275&amp;focus=kaska" aria-label="Kaska on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5517 758 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kaska lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5837 1014h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5837 1014h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Turkey. <a href="/atlas?year=-1275&amp;focus=kaska">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

